  "reason": "The top three experiments (config_029: 0.7250, config_007: 0.7207, config_010: 0.7150) all share scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile, forming a 2x2 grid over aggregation (transformer/avgpool) and fusion (concat/weighted). Three cells are filled; config_048 (avgpool + weighted) is the only missing cell. Evidence shows weighted fusion improves over concat by ~0.4% with transformer (0.7250 vs 0.7207) and avgpool underperforms transformer by ~0.6% with concat (0.7150 vs 0.7207). Testing avgpool+weighted clarifies whether the weighted-fusion gain is aggregation-independent or specific to transformer. If it outperforms config_029, we find a new best; if not, we confirm transformer+weighted as the optimal combination in this dominant family. With only 1 experiment remaining after this, completing the grid in the highest-performing region is the most informative and highest-expected-value use of the budget."
